Changelog: 11-10-2026 18:48:14

The checkout-only tools (BC250 Suite Releases, BC-250 Installer Tests) are always listed under Development only. A
portal without a checkout (installed from a release) shows them greyed, with Install and Uninstall off and a hint to
install the portal from the checkout (./install.sh in the repository); one installed earlier from a checkout still
opens. Until now such a portal did not list them at all.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 18:35:10

Release 0.9.6. more robust uninstall

Changelog: 11-10-2026 18:31:14

After a successful install or update, the app's other release folders in the portal's state (older releases, or a
staged checkout copy) are removed; only the one it was installed from stays, for its uninstaller. Until now every
release an app ever had stayed there. install.sh --uninstall without --purge keeps only the records and release
folders of the apps that stay installed (Bazzite Test's go with it), removes the state folder when none is left, and
the suite's data folder when it is empty. The installer test checks both (steps 3, 5 and 6).

Changelog: 11-10-2026 18:15:13

A portal from a checkout also lists BC-250 Installer Tests under Development only ([checkout.installer-tests] in
apps.toml). A [checkout.<name>] table may name its folder (folder = "...", default apps/<name>) for a tool that lives
elsewhere in the checkout, here tools/installer-tests/gui.

